131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (We analyzed three competitors in the dog apparel industry, including Canada Pooch, Lucy & Co., and Wild One, across Instagram, Facebook, and TikTok. The competitors have strong visual branding, using dogs wearing their products to showcase their apparel and accessories. Product demonstrations, seasonal content, lifestyle imagery, and creator- or customer-generated content are common themes among these brands. However, engagement varies significantly between platforms and brands, showing that a large following does not always translate into strong audience interaction. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (On Instagram, Canada Pooch has approximately 201k followers with an engagement rate of about 0.77%, while Lucy & Co. and Wild One also have large audiences but relatively low engagement rates. Canada Pooch and Wild One demonstrate strong visual identities, while Lucy & Co. uses eye-catching dog content and consistent branding. Across the competitors, product-focused posts and dogs modeling products are effective, but repeated promotional and seasonal content can become repetitive. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (The audit also identified several content gaps that create opportunities for differentiation. Competitors could use more interactive content, including questions/polls, and other posts made specifically to encourage comments and participation. There is also an opportunity for more relatable dog owner content and platform-specific short-form videos. Lucy & Co. and Wild One both identify opportunities to increase customer-generated content and community interaction, while Canada Pooch could benefit from using trends and relatable TikTok content.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (SUMMARY)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (HOW MY BOY BOONE WILL DIFFERENTIATE)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (Based on these findings, My Boy Boone would differentiate its dog hoodie content by combining strong product visuals with more interactive, relatable, and engaging content. Rather than relying on product promotion, My Boy Boone can use real dog owner content, humor, customer participation, and platform-specific trends and content to create a stronger connection with dog owners. This approach can help My Boy Boone stand out in a competitive dog apparel market while building a more engaged social media community. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
